/**
 * @mainpage MECHelangelo — Autonomous Gallery Robot
 *
 * @section overview Overview
 *
 * MECHelangelo is an autonomous, interactive gallery robot built on a
 * differential-drive mobile base.  It navigates a simulated or physical gallery
 * environment using a DVD-screensaver-style exploration strategy, detects
 * visitors with a camera and MediaPipe pose estimation, approaches them to a
 * safe interaction distance, and then mirrors their arm poses using a pair of
 * servo-driven arms controlled by a per-arm KNN classifier.
 *
 * The system runs under **ROS 2 Humble** on a **Raspberry Pi 5**.
 * On the physical robot a dedicated **Raspberry Pi 4** runs the camera pipeline
 * and exposes its output via HTTP.  In simulation an equivalent ROS node runs
 * the same pipeline using a Gazebo virtual camera and/or a USB laptop camera.
 *
 * The robot's name is a portmanteau of **MECH**anical and Micha**elangelo**,
 * reflecting its role as an interactive artistic robot that mirrors human
 * movement.
 *
 * @section architecture System Architecture
 *
 * @subsection arch_physical Physical robot data-flow
 * @code
 * YDLIDAR X4  ──/scan──────────────────────┐
 * Sense HAT   ──/imu───────────────────────┤
 *                                           ▼
 * Pi 4 Flask /state ──► pi4_bridge ──► mechelangelo_behaviour ──► /cmd_vel ──► ThunderBorg
 *                                                               └──► /arm/right_pose
 *                                                               └──► /arm/left_pose
 *                                                               └──► /interaction_active
 * @endcode
 *
 * @subsection arch_sim Simulation data-flow
 * @code
 * Gazebo camera ──► sim_pi4_state_camera (tracking)  ──► /sim_pi4/tracking_state ─┐
 * USB camera    ──► sim_pi4_state_camera (mimicry)   ──► /sim_pi4/mimicry_state  ─┤
 *                                                                                   ▼
 *                                                               sim_pi4_state_bridge
 *                                                                        │
 *                                               /human_tracking ◄────────┤
 *                                               /human_detected ◄────────┘
 *                                                        │
 * /scan (Gazebo) ──► mechelangelo_behaviour ─────────────┘
 *                           │
 *                           ├──► /cmd_vel ──► Gazebo differential drive
 *                           ├──► /arm/right_pose ──► sim_named_arm_pose_bridge
 *                           ├──► /arm/left_pose  ──► sim_named_arm_pose_bridge
 *                           └──► /interaction_active ──► sim_pi4_state_camera (mimicry gate)
 * @endcode
 *
 * @section packages ROS 2 Packages
 *
 * @subsection pkg_behaviour mechelangelo_behaviour
 *
 * | Attribute | Value |
 * |-----------|-------|
 * | Language  | C++ (ament_cmake) |
 * | Node name | `mechelangelo_behaviour` |
 * | Source    | `src/mechelangelo_behaviour/src/behaviour.cpp` |
 * | Header    | `src/mechelangelo_behaviour/src/behaviour.hpp` |
 *
 * The core navigation and human-interaction state machine.  Runs at **10 Hz**
 * and implements two high-level operating modes.
 *
 * **DVD-bounce exploration** cycles through NavigationState::SEARCHING →
 * NavigationState::ALIGNING → NavigationState::MOVING → NavigationState::STOPPED,
 * driving the robot around the gallery by selecting the longest clear LiDAR heading
 * after each wall stop.  The heading selection deliberately avoids the obstacle
 * that was just stopped for, biasing toward side-bounce angles (55°–150°)
 * so the robot covers the room rather than reversing.
 *
 * **Human approach and interaction** (NavigationState::HUMAN_DETECTED) fuses
 * the camera-supplied bearing with LiDAR range via a persistent target lock,
 * runs a dynamic-window arc planner to navigate to a 1.5 m arm-clearance bubble,
 * manages several recovery sub-modes (REPOSITION, ESCAPE, SETTLE, S-curve waypoint),
 * times a 30-second mimicry session, then returns to DVD exploration with a
 * detection cooldown to avoid immediately interrupting the next exploration run.
 *
 * Subscribed topics:
 * | Topic | Message type | Description |
 * |-------|-------------|-------------|
 * | `/scan` | `sensor_msgs/LaserScan` | Raw LiDAR scan (360°, YDLIDAR X4) |
 * | `/imu` | `sensor_msgs/Imu` | Orientation for IMU-confirmed turns |
 * | `/human_tracking` | `std_msgs/Float32MultiArray` | `[detected, centre_offset, dist_m]` |
 * | `/human_detected` | `std_msgs/Bool` | Edge-trigger for human lock acquire/loss |
 * | `/arm/mimicry_right_pose` | `std_msgs/String` | Forwarded to right arm during interaction |
 * | `/arm/mimicry_left_pose` | `std_msgs/String` | Forwarded to left arm during interaction |
 *
 * Published topics:
 * | Topic | Message type | Description |
 * |-------|-------------|-------------|
 * | `/cmd_vel` | `geometry_msgs/Twist` | Velocity command to base |
 * | `/arm/right_pose` | `std_msgs/String` | Named pose for right arm |
 * | `/arm/left_pose` | `std_msgs/String` | Named pose for left arm |
 * | `/interaction_active` | `std_msgs/Bool` | Latched interaction gate |
 * | `/voice_prompt` | `std_msgs/String` | Text for the future audio system |
 * | `/scan_filtered` | `sensor_msgs/LaserScan` | Noise-filtered scan (debug) |
 * | `/behaviour_obstacle_markers` | `visualization_msgs/MarkerArray` | Blocking segments (RViz debug) |
 *
 * ROS parameters:
 * | Parameter | Default | Description |
 * |-----------|---------|-------------|
 * | `stop_distance_m` | `1.5` | Wall stop distance in metres. Set to `0.75` for the physical robot. |
 * | `approach_arm_pose_name` | `"arm_down"` | Named pose sent to both arms during non-interaction states. |
 *
 * @subsection pkg_perception mechelangelo_perception
 *
 * | Attribute | Value |
 * |-----------|-------|
 * | Language  | Python (ament_python) |
 * | Source    | `src/mechelangelo_perception/mechelangelo_perception/` |
 *
 * The perception pipeline bridges camera data into ROS topics consumed by the
 * behaviour node.  Contains the following nodes:
 *
 * | Python file | Node name | Role |
 * |-------------|-----------|------|
 * | `sim_pi4_state_camera.py` | `sim_pi4_state_camera` | MediaPipe pose detection (tracking or mimicry role) |
 * | `sim_pi4_state_bridge.py` | `sim_pi4_state_bridge` | Combines tracking + mimicry JSON state into `/human_tracking` |
 * | `pi4_bridge.py` | `pi4_bridge` | Physical-robot HTTP poller: Pi 4 `/state` → ROS topics |
 * | `sim_interaction_gate.py` | `sim_interaction_gate` | Emits `/interaction_active` when range + centring criteria are met |
 * | `sim_named_arm_pose_bridge.py` | `sim_named_arm_pose_bridge` | Converts named arm poses to Gazebo 8-joint trajectories |
 * | `dual_ultrasonic.py` | `dual_ultrasonic_node` | GPIO HY-SRF05 / HC-SR04 ultrasonic distance driver (physical robot) |
 *
 * **sim_pi4_state_camera** (`--role tracking`): Subscribes to the Gazebo robot
 * camera image topic, runs MediaPipe Pose every other frame, implements a
 * LockState tracker that acquires and holds a single-person lock (with a 5-second
 * grace period on visibility loss), and publishes a JSON state blob containing
 * `turn_cmd` (`TURN_LEFT` / `TURN_RIGHT` / `STOP`) and `locked`.
 * A Flask debug server exposes a live MJPEG stream and the current state.
 *
 * **sim_pi4_state_camera** (`--role mimicry`): Reads a USB/laptop camera,
 * extracts 11 joint-angle/position features from MediaPipe Pose, classifies
 * each arm with an ArmKNN weighted KNN classifier (k=9, majority-vote window of
 * 10 frames), and publishes confirmed pose names — gated behind
 * `/interaction_active` so the arms only move once the robot has arrived.
 * KNN training data is persisted as JSON files on disk and can be extended at
 * runtime via HTTP `GET /record/right/<pose>` and `/record/left/<pose>`.
 *
 * **ArmKNN**: An 11-feature, weighted Euclidean KNN classifier.  Features:
 * shoulder angle, elbow angle, upper-arm Z depth, forearm Z depth, wrist
 * relative Y/X, elbow relative Y/X, forearm 2D angle, upper-arm 2D angle,
 * elbow from shoulder midpoint.  Feature weights emphasise elbow-from-centre
 * (weight 4.0) and elbow position (2.5) over pure angles.
 *
 * **sim_pi4_state_bridge**: Mirrors `pi4_bridge.py` but reads from
 * `/sim_pi4/tracking_state` and `/sim_pi4/mimicry_state` ROS String topics
 * instead of polling HTTP.  Converts the tri-state `turn_cmd` into a smoothed
 * floating-point `centre_offset` (alpha = 0.35) for the behaviour node.
 *
 * **pi4_bridge** (physical robot only): Polls `http://172.20.10.3:5000/state`
 * at 10 Hz with a 300 ms timeout.  Translates `TURN_LEFT` / `TURN_RIGHT` /
 * `STOP` into a centre_offset and publishes `/human_tracking`,
 * `/human_detected`, `/arm/right_pose`, `/arm/left_pose`, `/arm/turn`, and
 * `/arm/locked`.  Falls back to a safe "human lost" state on any HTTP failure.
 *
 * **sim_interaction_gate** (simulation helper): An independent node that
 * evaluates whether the robot has reached a human-interaction pose and publishes
 * `/interaction_active` accordingly.  Used in simulation runs that do not rely
 * on the behaviour node's internal interaction-hold logic.
 *
 * **sim_named_arm_pose_bridge**: Converts named pose strings (e.g. `"salute"`)
 * received on `/arm/right_pose` and `/arm/left_pose` into a full 8-joint
 * `trajectory_msgs/JointTrajectory` message for the Gazebo arm controllers.
 * Uses a servo-degree → joint-radian conversion that maps the physical LX-16A
 * servo range (0–240°, centre 120°) to ±2.09 rad.
 *
 * **dual_ultrasonic**: GPIO driver for two front-facing HY-SRF05 / HC-SR04
 * ultrasonic sensors.  Alternates triggering to avoid cross-talk, applies a
 * median filter over the last 5 valid readings, and publishes
 * `sensor_msgs/Range` on `/ultrasonic/left` and `/ultrasonic/right`.
 * Echo lines must be voltage-divided (10 kΩ / 10 kΩ) before reaching the Pi GPIO.
 *
 * @subsection pkg_base mechelangelo_base_driver
 *
 * | Attribute | Value |
 * |-----------|-------|
 * | Language  | Python (ament_python) |
 * | Node name | `mechelangelo_base_driver` |
 * | Source    | `src/mechelangelo_base_driver/mechelangelo_base_driver/base_driver.py` |
 *
 * Subscribes to `/cmd_vel` (`geometry_msgs/Twist`) and drives the robot's two
 * DC motors via the **PiBorg ThunderBorg** I²C motor controller.  Converts
 * linear and angular velocity into open-loop left/right motor percentages using
 * configurable max-speed parameters.  A software watchdog cuts motor power if
 * `/cmd_vel` is silent for more than a configurable timeout.  The ThunderBorg
 * I²C comms failsafe is also configured so the motors cut out if the Pi loses
 * the bus.
 *
 * @subsection pkg_bringup mechelangelo_bringup
 *
 * | Attribute | Value |
 * |-----------|-------|
 * | Language  | Python launch files |
 * | Source    | `src/mechelangelo_bringup/launch/` |
 *
 * Top-level launch files for bringing up the physical robot:
 *
 * | File | Purpose |
 * |------|---------|
 * | `robot.launch.py` | Full physical bringup: URDF, LiDAR, IMU, base driver, behaviour, perception |
 * | `physical_autonomous.launch.py` | Autonomous physical run, sets `stop_distance_m:=0.75` |
 *
 * Simulation-specific launch files live in `mechelangelo_gazebo`.
 * Custom Gazebo SDF environment models (gallery walls, floor, barrels, statues,
 * artwork textures) also reside here under `Models/`.
 *
 * @subsection pkg_lidar mechelangelo_lidar_driver
 *
 * | Attribute | Value |
 * |-----------|-------|
 * | Language  | Python (ament_python) |
 * | Node name | `mechelangelo_lidar_driver` |
 *
 * Driver for the **YDLIDAR X4** 2-D LiDAR.  Publishes `/scan`
 * (`sensor_msgs/LaserScan`) at ~10 Hz with a 360° sweep.
 * The behaviour node runs a two-stage noise filter (local neighbour test +
 * segment-extraction test) on this scan before using it for obstacle avoidance
 * and human range estimation.
 *
 * @subsection pkg_imu mechelangelo_imu_driver
 *
 * | Attribute | Value |
 * |-----------|-------|
 * | Language  | Python (ament_python) |
 * | Node name | `mechelangelo_imu_driver` |
 *
 * Driver for the **Raspberry Pi Sense HAT** (LSM9DS1 9-DOF IMU, RTIMULib).
 * The IMU link is at (0, 0, 0.37 m) relative to `base_link`.
 *
 * Published topics:
 * | Topic | Type | Content |
 * |-------|------|---------|
 * | `/imu` | `sensor_msgs/Imu` | Orientation quaternion + angular velocity |
 * | `/mag` | `sensor_msgs/MagneticField` | Magnetometer vector |
 * | `/pressure` | `sensor_msgs/FluidPressure` | Barometric pressure |
 * | `/humidity` | `sensor_msgs/RelativeHumidity` | Relative humidity |
 * | `/temp_p` | `sensor_msgs/Temperature` | Temperature (pressure sensor) |
 * | `/temp_h` | `sensor_msgs/Temperature` | Temperature (humidity sensor) |
 *
 * @subsection pkg_description mechelangelo_description
 *
 * | Attribute | Value |
 * |-----------|-------|
 * | Language  | URDF / xacro |
 * | Source    | `src/mechelangelo_description/urdf/` |
 *
 * Robot URDF description files.
 *
 * | File | Content |
 * |------|---------|
 * | `mechelangelo_final.urdf` | Complete robot: base + dual 4-DOF arms + sensors |
 * | `mechelangelo_base.urdf` | Base-only (no arms) |
 * | `mechelangelo_arm.urdf` | Single-arm test model |
 * | `mechelangelo_dual_arms.urdf` | Dual-arm test model |
 *
 * Arm meshes (STL / DAE) are in `meshes/Arms/`.  Base meshes are in
 * `meshes/base_final/`.
 *
 * @subsection pkg_gazebo mechelangelo_gazebo
 *
 * | Attribute | Value |
 * |-----------|-------|
 * | Language  | Python launch files, SDF world / model files |
 * | Source    | `src/mechelangelo_gazebo/` |
 *
 * Gazebo Classic simulation environment.
 *
 * **Models** (in `models/`):
 * - `gallery_floor`, `empty_gallery_floor`, `empty_gallery_walls` — gallery geometry.
 * - `barrels`, `walls` (with artwork textures), `statues` — gallery props.
 * - Eight human NPC models: `human_female_1` – `human_female_4`,
 *   `human_male_1` – `human_male_4`.
 * - `mechelangelo_dual_arms` — the robot model with arm meshes and controllers.
 *
 * **Launch files**:
 * | File | Purpose |
 * |------|---------|
 * | `mechelangelo.launch.py` | Full simulation: gallery world + robot |
 * | `environment.launch.py` | Gallery world only (no robot) |
 * | `empty_gallery.launch.py` | Empty gallery (no props/artwork) |
 * | `mechelangelo_full_mimicry_sim.launch.py` | Combined sim approach + USB mimicry camera |
 * | `environment_arm.launch.py` | Arm-only test environment |
 *
 * Arm joint-trajectory controller parameters are in `config/arm_controllers.yaml`.
 *
 * @section topic_map Complete Key Topic Map
 *
 * @code
 * [YDLIDAR X4]        /scan                    ──► mechelangelo_behaviour
 * [Sense HAT]         /imu                     ──► mechelangelo_behaviour
 * [pi4_bridge /       /human_tracking           ──► mechelangelo_behaviour
 *  sim bridge]        /human_detected           ──► mechelangelo_behaviour
 * [mechelangelo_       /cmd_vel                 ──► base_driver / Gazebo
 *  behaviour]          /arm/right_pose          ──► arm bridge / Dynamixel
 *                      /arm/left_pose           ──► arm bridge / Dynamixel
 *                      /interaction_active      ──► sim_pi4_state_camera (mimicry)
 *                      /voice_prompt            ──► (future audio node)
 *                      /scan_filtered           ──► RViz debug
 *                      /behaviour_obstacle_markers ──► RViz debug
 * [sim arm bridge]     /set_joint_trajectory    ──► Gazebo joint controllers
 * [dual_ultrasonic]    /ultrasonic/left         ──► (available to behaviour)
 *                      /ultrasonic/right        ──► (available to behaviour)
 * @endcode
 */
